How would an acceptable replacement NetHack scoring
system work?

As stated off-thread, I want to open this can of
worms again and see if any more consensus building
is possible.

There is fairly general agreement, supported by lots
of overwhelmingly convincing evidence not worth
repeating here, both that NetHack's current scoring
system is broken as it stands, and also that it has
been overtaken by new ideas of what constitutes
playing the game well.

Now, playing the game in a way the community agrees
is "playing well" is a near guarantee NOT to end up
on the high scores table of current multi-player
servers, where our two tournaments and much of the
community's remaining competitive play takes place.

The blocking issue in agreeing on a new scoring
system has always been lack of consensus on what
scoring mechanism(s) would accurately reflect "good
play" in today's understanding, while working well
in both of two essential ways:

* Scoring as a measure of progress for non-ascension
  games, so that the player is somehow given a pat
  on the back for getting closer to the game's
  nominal end goal.

* Scoring as a measure of merit for ascension games,
  that agrees with having behaved in ways that give
  "bragging rights" in an ascension posting.

It isn't all that obvious that working toward a
single, linearly orderable score is possible, but if
high score tables that rank games are going to
happen, and tables be of limiited capacity so that
some games eventually get kicked off the bottom,
that's the only kind of scoring that will suffice.

An obvious alternative is to have N _different_
ordering methods (most wealth, most conducts, fewest
kills + collateral deaths, most kills, most single
kills, most extinctions, etc.) , and maintain N
different high score tables, on zero to N of which
any particular game might earn a spot. That's really
an attractive possible way to go, just because it
gives players lots of chances to shine in lots of
ways, like tournaments do now, but not-so-fun maybe
for Nethack server maintainers.

Many, many, many possible components that _could_ go
into a score exist. I'll throw out a bucketfull,
tersely stated, unsorted and undifferentiated as to
quality, then try to stay out of the way while they
get discussed, if anyone is interested.

Please _first_ take time to do postings extending
this list without commenting on the merit pro or con
of its existing or your additional entries.

After all _your_ suggestions for score components
are visible for consideration, take time in separate
postings to comment on merits. Preferably, discuss
only one or two components per posting, in depth,
rather than everything in one big posting, and keep
postings terse. Keep changing the subject lines to
make it easy to trace followups about those
particular components through the whole thread, like
